WEBVTT

00:01:38.807 --> 00:01:40.183
The moment we're born,

00:01:41.184 --> 00:01:44.020
a new star appears in the sky, too.

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:45.563
It's called a Guardian Star.

00:01:45.647 --> 00:01:46.898
Which one is mine?

00:01:48.316 --> 00:01:49.651
I don't know,

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:54.280
but you're the only one
who can get that star to shine.

00:01:54.364 --> 00:01:56.866
Then I should be able
to recognize it for myself.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.701
Don't believe what he says.

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:02.122
Hey, Jack!
Don't try to distract us with that story.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.833
Where are the shooting stars?

00:02:04.916 --> 00:02:07.544
You promised us it'd be
a once-in-a-lifetime celestial show!

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.212
I know!

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:13.258
It's weird, we should be
able to see it right about now.

00:02:17.846 --> 00:02:19.222
It's getting cold, wanna go back?

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:20.682
What? Wait!

00:02:20.765 --> 00:02:22.433
I'll get a telescope from the clubroom!

00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:23.643
What? I'm over it.

00:02:23.726 --> 00:02:24.853
Hold on, just wait!

00:02:30.441 --> 00:02:32.235
My star is…

00:02:36.239 --> 00:02:41.119
A TEEN'S NEVER-ENDING ALARM

00:03:13.985 --> 00:03:16.404
TO TEM

00:03:49.854 --> 00:03:51.981
You gotta believe me!

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:54.108
There definitely was something there!

00:03:54.192 --> 00:03:57.320
The shooting stars were a bust,
so you're trying to distract us.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.864
-What?
-But I've heard of that before.

00:03:59.948 --> 00:04:04.077
Supposedly, there's a six-eyed monster
that appears at our school.

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:06.621
Well, good for you, Jack.

00:04:06.704 --> 00:04:09.582
You saw that monster, case closed.

00:04:09.666 --> 00:04:11.876
You can mock me because you didn't see it.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:17.257
Hey… By any chance,
was that in front of Lecture Room 2?

00:04:18.633 --> 00:04:20.885
Yeah… But what about it?

00:04:20.969 --> 00:04:22.345
What? Don't you know?

00:04:23.012 --> 00:04:24.806
It's Tem's ghost!

00:04:25.473 --> 00:04:26.641
What?

00:04:26.724 --> 00:04:29.352
Six months passed
since the devouring incident

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:32.021
and the perpetrator still
hasn't been caught, right?

00:04:32.563 --> 00:04:36.276
They say if you go to
Lecture Room 2 in the middle of the night,

00:04:36.359 --> 00:04:39.654
you'll hear Tem's footsteps.

00:04:39.737 --> 00:04:42.073
What? How do you know it's Tem?

00:04:42.156 --> 00:04:43.741
Who else would it be?

00:04:44.492 --> 00:04:50.331
Plus, a student who was often seen
around there is now missing.

00:04:51.708 --> 00:04:53.334
What? Who?

00:04:53.918 --> 00:04:55.169
It's Rouis!

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:59.799
It's got to be related
to why he doesn't come to schoo--

00:05:01.926 --> 00:05:02.844
Sorry.

00:05:02.927 --> 00:05:05.054
Come on.

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:07.056
Read the room.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:11.894
But this sure is ridiculous,
we're second-years in high school.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:13.771
You can say that
because you didn't see it.

00:05:13.855 --> 00:05:16.858
What are you doing after school today?
Can I see you?

00:05:16.941 --> 00:05:18.234
Okay, at the usual spot.

00:05:21.863 --> 00:05:22.905
During breaks,

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:26.576
we occasionally meet up and chat.

00:05:27.702 --> 00:05:28.786
I invite her.

00:05:29.704 --> 00:05:31.456
She chooses the place.

00:05:33.207 --> 00:05:37.587
Gosh, Legoshi,
you don't have to worry that much.

00:05:38.212 --> 00:05:40.590
There are rumors like that
among the third-years, too.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:42.550
That something's living in the walls.

00:05:43.217 --> 00:05:46.179
Or there was a student who
killed himself in the bathroom long ago.

00:05:46.262 --> 00:05:47.513
-Really?
-Yup.

00:05:47.597 --> 00:05:50.433
Plus, you know I'm always by myself,

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:53.186
but I've never encountered anything scary.

00:05:59.484 --> 00:06:00.943
-Sorry.
-No, it's okay.

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:03.279
Well, we got to meet
each other because of that.

00:06:06.908 --> 00:06:09.869
I've been curious about this for a while.

00:06:09.952 --> 00:06:11.079
What is it?

00:06:11.162 --> 00:06:12.747
Why do we always meet up here?

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.504
Precisely because of that.

00:06:19.587 --> 00:06:21.130
What do you mean?

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:22.548
Okay, well…

00:06:23.758 --> 00:06:24.759
Listen.

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:29.472
In the world of small animals,
rumors spread like wild fire, and plus,

00:06:30.098 --> 00:06:31.557
they linger for a long time.

00:06:31.641 --> 00:06:33.851
Are you being bullied?

00:06:33.935 --> 00:06:35.853
Since you spent the night out with a wolf?

00:06:35.937 --> 00:06:38.564
I've always been bullied.
It's just charged up right now.

00:06:38.648 --> 00:06:41.651
-I'm worried. I want to help you--
-Stop!

00:06:42.985 --> 00:06:44.987
I really appreciate the thought, though.

00:06:45.947 --> 00:06:49.033
If you acted bold,
maybe the bullying would stop.

00:06:51.619 --> 00:06:54.539
But it's weird to be acting bold, too.

00:06:55.206 --> 00:06:56.707
Right?

00:06:56.791 --> 00:07:00.503
Because our relationship is…

00:07:02.171 --> 00:07:03.381
You know?

00:07:04.674 --> 00:07:06.050
Yeah…

00:07:06.968 --> 00:07:09.428
We don't have to change anything, right?

00:07:09.512 --> 00:07:12.223
It's so much fun just chatting like this.

00:07:12.306 --> 00:07:13.349
I'm serious.

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:19.605
Are we not together?

00:07:21.149 --> 00:07:22.775
This is too complicated.

00:07:23.401 --> 00:07:26.320
I assumed we were,
just with the texts and meet-ups.

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:31.784
I'll…

00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:34.245
be stronger.

00:07:35.037 --> 00:07:36.664
I said that,

00:07:37.373 --> 00:07:39.375
but I haven't actually done anything.

00:07:40.418 --> 00:07:44.380
Plus Hal must be worried about Rouis, too.

00:07:45.298 --> 00:07:46.299
Hey, Legoshi!

00:07:46.883 --> 00:07:48.509
-You listening?
-Yes!

00:07:48.593 --> 00:07:49.802
In any case,

00:07:49.886 --> 00:07:50.970
around this time of year,

00:07:51.053 --> 00:07:53.681
we would be casting
for the autumn performance,

00:07:53.764 --> 00:07:56.893
but with Rouis missing,
we should wait longer and see--

00:07:56.976 --> 00:08:01.189
You mean we wait
and do nothing until Rouis is found?

00:08:01.272 --> 00:08:02.106
Yeah…

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:04.442
If he were here,
he'd probably arrange for stand-ins.

00:08:04.525 --> 00:08:07.445
There's no point talking
about someone who's not here.

00:08:07.528 --> 00:08:08.863
I wonder if he's sick.

00:08:08.946 --> 00:08:10.948
He doesn't seem
to be the type to get sick.

00:08:11.032 --> 00:08:14.452
The last time I saw him was the day
before the Festival of the Meteor.

00:08:18.789 --> 00:08:20.166
Rouis…

00:08:37.058 --> 00:08:38.809
Never mind, Durham.

00:08:38.893 --> 00:08:40.478
Let's go back.

00:08:42.313 --> 00:08:44.065
It's gonna be okay.

00:08:44.148 --> 00:08:46.234
There's not going to be anything there.

00:08:46.317 --> 00:08:48.861
Let's get Jack to buy us milk.

00:08:48.945 --> 00:08:55.785
ROUIS IS MISSING!!

00:09:00.414 --> 00:09:02.208
See?

00:09:02.291 --> 00:09:04.001
There's nothing here.

00:09:04.085 --> 00:09:07.338
It'd be a shame if Tem
were still lingering around here, too.

00:09:07.421 --> 00:09:10.424
Well, yeah, you're right.

00:09:10.508 --> 00:09:13.386
Now take a picture for proof.

00:09:13.469 --> 00:09:15.930
Gosh, fine then.

00:09:16.013 --> 00:09:17.139
Yay!

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:20.810
All right! Three, two, one!

00:09:24.855 --> 00:09:26.399
What are you doing?

00:09:26.482 --> 00:09:29.443
Behind you… just now…

00:09:33.364 --> 00:09:34.574
There's nothing there.

00:09:35.241 --> 00:09:36.659
I swear it was there!

00:09:36.742 --> 00:09:38.077
It showed up in the pic.

00:09:49.463 --> 00:09:51.215
Wait! Don't leave me!

00:09:57.179 --> 00:09:58.931
I wonder if they're okay.

00:10:01.058 --> 00:10:03.060
-What's up?
-Nothing.

00:10:06.188 --> 00:10:09.025
It appeared!

00:10:09.108 --> 00:10:10.109
PR DEPT

00:10:10.192 --> 00:10:13.321
No! There's no way
I'd publish a childish article titled

00:10:13.404 --> 00:10:16.699
"There Might be a Ghost
in the Lecture Room"!

00:10:16.782 --> 00:10:20.661
With no photos of Rouis,
business has been slow already.

00:10:20.745 --> 00:10:23.581
No, please, look at this.
I even got injured.

00:10:23.664 --> 00:10:24.874
You tripped by yourself.

00:10:24.957 --> 00:10:26.626
Will you let a freak like this go?

00:10:26.709 --> 00:10:28.711
It's not about
whether it's dangerous or not.

00:10:28.794 --> 00:10:30.755
It's about whether it sells or not!

00:10:30.838 --> 00:10:35.676
Hey, by any chance,
does that thing make strange sounds?

00:10:36.677 --> 00:10:37.762
Something like this?

00:10:37.845 --> 00:10:39.805
-No.
-It didn't make that sound…

00:10:40.681 --> 00:10:43.017
But we heard footsteps, right?

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:45.561
If we heard footsteps, it must have feet.

00:10:45.645 --> 00:10:48.147
So, that means it's not a ghost.

00:10:48.731 --> 00:10:51.359
Please investigate this
before there's another victim.

00:10:51.442 --> 00:10:54.153
Well, all right then… Not!
I'm not a detective, you know!

00:10:54.236 --> 00:10:56.447
It can be the murderer
from the devouring incident.

00:10:56.530 --> 00:10:58.866
That's right.
That would be a big scoop, wouldn't it?

00:10:58.949 --> 00:11:01.994
You're right… Not!
Just get out of my sight!

00:11:10.544 --> 00:11:11.545
Excuse me!

00:11:17.426 --> 00:11:18.469
Hey.

00:11:30.981 --> 00:11:32.441
Rouis?

00:11:32.525 --> 00:11:34.568
It's been a while, Legoshi.

00:11:37.488 --> 00:11:38.614
Why?

00:11:39.698 --> 00:11:41.742
-Since when?
-Since just now.

00:11:44.328 --> 00:11:47.540
Where have you been for two months?

00:11:49.708 --> 00:11:52.128
Really? Two months?

00:11:53.796 --> 00:11:55.047
They were long, weren't they?

00:11:55.673 --> 00:11:57.091
I don't understand.

00:11:57.800 --> 00:11:59.093
He's so calm.

00:11:59.885 --> 00:12:01.971
I have so much to discuss with him.

00:12:03.973 --> 00:12:06.434
But this vibe is stopping me
from getting any closer.

00:12:08.936 --> 00:12:09.979
Rouis!

00:12:10.062 --> 00:12:13.107
-You're back!
-Where the heck have you been?

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:14.525
I'm sorry to have worried you.

00:12:14.608 --> 00:12:18.737
We'll get into that later.
I'm just so happy!

00:12:18.821 --> 00:12:23.492
It's all right now, President.
Just process this for me.

00:12:23.576 --> 00:12:24.577
RESIGNATION LETTER

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:25.494
What?

00:12:26.912 --> 00:12:30.499
I came to give you this today.
Thanks for everything.

00:12:31.083 --> 00:12:32.001
You're quitting?

00:12:32.084 --> 00:12:33.419
What do you mean?

00:12:33.502 --> 00:12:36.046
The Drama Club can't go on without you--

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:37.590
How nostalgic.

00:12:39.508 --> 00:12:45.264
Had I been on stage
all the time in such a cheesy light?

00:12:47.057 --> 00:12:49.727
While the audience was captivated by me,

00:12:49.810 --> 00:12:52.480
I could see in their eyes
that they were anticipating my fall.

00:12:54.148 --> 00:12:55.733
I remember it vividly.

00:13:03.616 --> 00:13:07.161
The light and dark
reversed brilliantly, didn't it, Legoshi?

00:13:09.246 --> 00:13:11.957
Good luck struggling in the faint light.

00:13:13.501 --> 00:13:15.878
I chose a different way to fight.

00:13:18.672 --> 00:13:19.673
Rouis!

00:13:23.844 --> 00:13:25.137
Rouis.

00:13:27.306 --> 00:13:29.892
Today is "Biology Day."

00:13:29.975 --> 00:13:32.728
Since it tends to get crowded
right before closing time…

00:13:32.811 --> 00:13:33.896
Here.

00:13:33.979 --> 00:13:35.356
…please complete it early.

00:13:36.065 --> 00:13:37.191
Again…

00:13:37.942 --> 00:13:38.984
Okay!

00:13:39.068 --> 00:13:43.364
Since it tends to get crowded
right before closing time,

00:13:43.989 --> 00:13:45.991
please complete early.

00:13:49.578 --> 00:13:52.873
ADLER - ROUIS

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:58.170
I'm glad he's safe for now.

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:02.550
The light and dark
reversed brilliantly, didn't it, Legoshi?

00:14:04.843 --> 00:14:06.011
What does that mean?

00:14:06.095 --> 00:14:07.054
Come on, let's go.

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:11.183
ROUIS

00:14:17.106 --> 00:14:23.112
BIOLOGY LAB

00:14:23.195 --> 00:14:24.196
Juno!

00:14:29.743 --> 00:14:31.912
Do you know anything about Rouis?

00:14:35.666 --> 00:14:38.335
Please stop playing with my heart!

00:14:38.919 --> 00:14:39.753
What?

00:14:39.837 --> 00:14:44.425
Since I told you how I felt about you,
I can't look you in the eye.

00:14:46.552 --> 00:14:53.267
Plus, you gave me an ambiguous answer
and just left me there.

00:14:53.851 --> 00:14:54.852
You're strong.

00:14:55.728 --> 00:15:00.399
I want you to keep up that manliness
and continue to lead everyone. Bye.

00:15:00.482 --> 00:15:01.483
What?

00:15:02.318 --> 00:15:03.986
I understand what happened.

00:15:04.069 --> 00:15:08.991
My love can't beat your disgust
toward the same species, right?

00:15:09.992 --> 00:15:13.621
But at this rate,
I can't move on even if I wanted to.

00:15:13.704 --> 00:15:17.583
Please reject me right here, right now!

00:15:17.666 --> 00:15:18.918
Please!

00:15:24.715 --> 00:15:26.425
Don't cry, Juno.

00:15:27.009 --> 00:15:31.680
I don't have the right to say this,
but I think we're actually quite similar.

00:15:31.764 --> 00:15:34.350
We're a bit stubborn
and forceful at times.

00:15:34.433 --> 00:15:35.768
I meant it in a good way.

00:15:35.851 --> 00:15:39.355
Well, why don't we go to
the Wolf Room and bathe in the moonlight?

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:44.026
Let's go, okay?

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:57.748
Juno!

00:16:00.084 --> 00:16:03.337
What's with this cheerful atmosphere?

00:16:03.921 --> 00:16:07.132
We were just talking about you.
We're all really grateful, you know?

00:16:08.133 --> 00:16:10.594
Grateful? What do you mean?

00:16:10.678 --> 00:16:12.846
Your speech at the Festival of the Meteor.

00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:15.516
The herbivores look at us differently now.

00:16:15.599 --> 00:16:17.434
They don't get scared
when we approach them.

00:16:17.518 --> 00:16:20.104
It's all because of you. Thanks a lot!

00:16:22.815 --> 00:16:25.818
I had no idea.

00:16:29.238 --> 00:16:30.531
Hey, Legoshi.

00:16:31.657 --> 00:16:34.201
I admit that I'm stubborn.

00:16:35.703 --> 00:16:40.040
But in terms of living forcefully,
nobody surpasses you.

00:16:42.251 --> 00:16:44.378
Juno, you just might be the next Beastar!

00:16:44.461 --> 00:16:45.963
Please, don't be too hasty.

00:16:46.046 --> 00:16:48.632
-With Rouis gone, it's possible!
-Yeah!

00:16:48.716 --> 00:16:49.717
It is!

00:16:51.719 --> 00:16:53.554
She represents justice here.

00:16:54.888 --> 00:16:58.100
Here in a place
where there are no herbivores.

00:16:59.101 --> 00:17:00.269
TEACHERS ROOM

00:17:00.352 --> 00:17:01.812
A FEW DAYS LATER

00:17:02.396 --> 00:17:04.148
Where's the principal today?

00:17:04.231 --> 00:17:05.607
He's gone.

00:17:05.691 --> 00:17:10.195
He left for the Council of Living Beings
with a dejected face.

00:17:10.696 --> 00:17:11.905
The Council?

00:17:12.698 --> 00:17:14.283
How many years has it been?

00:17:16.035 --> 00:17:19.038
And this isn't just another Council.

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:21.749
The leaders of all species
are gathering together

00:17:21.832 --> 00:17:25.669
to select the Beastar
of Cherryton School from the students.

00:17:26.295 --> 00:17:29.798
The Beastar who hasn't been selected
at this school for the past five years.

00:17:29.882 --> 00:17:30.924
ROUIS - JUNO

00:17:34.428 --> 00:17:35.471
GHOST EYEBALL CAUGHT!!

00:17:35.554 --> 00:17:40.059
"A guinea pig, parenthesis first-year,
who used the air vents to get around

00:17:40.142 --> 00:17:43.312
started pulling pranks to scare students."

00:17:44.354 --> 00:17:45.647
What?

00:17:45.731 --> 00:17:48.525
Damn it! We were fooled by a first-year!

00:17:48.609 --> 00:17:51.570
Was that photo taken
with the camera you set up, Boss?

00:17:51.653 --> 00:17:52.654
Yeah.

00:17:52.738 --> 00:17:55.741
The shutter goes off when it senses heat.

00:17:55.824 --> 00:17:59.536
And then,
it sends the picture to my phone.

00:18:05.542 --> 00:18:06.585
What's that?

00:18:08.253 --> 00:18:11.590
Maybe a cockroach or something
passed by in front of the camera.

00:18:11.673 --> 00:18:14.051
What idiot would be fooled by this?

00:18:14.134 --> 00:18:16.345
Forget that, did you see Juno?

00:18:16.428 --> 00:18:19.973
Yeah, I did!
She's something else, isn't she?

00:18:20.057 --> 00:18:22.726
She's so popular
even though she's only a first-year.

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:24.478
-I had my eye on her.
-You, too? Me too!

00:18:24.561 --> 00:18:26.230
MEET MISS CHERRYTON CANDIDATES!

00:18:38.367 --> 00:18:42.746
No matter how the things around me change,
I'm confident that I'll stay on my path.

00:18:51.421 --> 00:18:55.092
Let's say Juno rises to
the top of the school.

00:18:56.218 --> 00:18:57.511
I…

00:19:07.521 --> 00:19:10.399
Good luck struggling in the faint light.

00:19:11.233 --> 00:19:14.486
My conviction to live strong.

00:19:15.028 --> 00:19:16.321
What?

00:19:16.405 --> 00:19:19.324
Could it mean to live quietly "as usual"?

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:25.372
Did I just find
my life's purpose at age 17?

00:19:32.588 --> 00:19:36.383
But, well, this means that
the monster doesn't exist then, right?

00:19:36.466 --> 00:19:37.885
That's right.

00:19:37.968 --> 00:19:40.596
Now you can go
to the bathroom alone, Jack.

00:19:40.679 --> 00:19:43.265
You didn't have to say that
in front of everyone.

00:19:43.348 --> 00:19:44.933
No, it exists.

00:19:45.517 --> 00:19:46.560
Can't you hear it?

00:19:47.144 --> 00:19:49.104
-There's something in this room.
-What?

00:19:49.188 --> 00:19:51.481
-What?
-No, no! That's too scary!

00:19:52.107 --> 00:19:55.152
But I can really hear this "shaaa" sound.

00:19:56.528 --> 00:19:57.571
I feel eyes on me, too.

00:19:59.865 --> 00:20:02.117
Come on, Jack. You're his friend, right?

00:20:03.285 --> 00:20:08.040
The ringing in your ear is caused
by stress and lack of sleep.

00:20:17.257 --> 00:20:20.928
I'll go borrow some tools
when I go get the laundry.

00:20:21.929 --> 00:20:23.138
I gotta fix this up.

00:20:26.099 --> 00:20:30.312
What was that?
He moved like a trained assassin.

00:20:43.367 --> 00:20:45.494
Will you please
introduce yourself already?

00:20:46.411 --> 00:20:48.330
I sense you all the time these days.

00:20:49.206 --> 00:20:50.249
What is it?

00:20:50.916 --> 00:20:53.335
At this rate,
people will think I'm a weirdo.

00:20:54.711 --> 00:20:57.881
You can't really be
that six-eyed ghost, can you?

00:21:05.681 --> 00:21:11.228
It seems that
the time has come to reveal myself.

00:22:17.002 --> 00:22:21.715
I'm starting to understand
the reason why I was born a wolf.

00:22:21.798 --> 00:22:25.010
My claws and fangs are just for you.

00:22:25.093 --> 00:22:27.471
I'll be a beast of yours.

00:22:45.947 --> 00:22:50.952
Subtitle translation by: Kanako Murakoshi
